Mark Healey <die@spammer.die> writes:

> Ok, the directory permissions and ownerships are correct owned by root:root
> with rwxr-xr-x all the way down to nethackdir which is owned by
> games:games.  

My nethackdir has group bin.

> all the files in that directory are games:games except the bones which is
> root:games.  It seems that this confirms what I assumed in my other post,
> that the userid isn't being set to games.

Group bin for all the files there, too, and for the bones subdirectory.
And the binary has the suid bit set (-rwsr-xr-x).
Maybe you have it sgid instead, and that may be the problem since you
don't have the group write permission for the directory.
Have you changed some of these settings in the Makefile?
The way it is in the original tarball, make install sets the suid bit and
changes the group to bin. You CAN have it sgid instead, but that requires
group write permissions.

